{
  "format": "aavanam-vector/v1",
  "title": "A delta bundle lists the withheld digest of a base reading that is the parent of one of its excerpts",
  "clauses": [
    "BUN-DLT-2",
    "BUN-DLT-4",
    "BUN-DLT-5",
    "BUN-RED-4",
    "BUN-IMP-9",
    "BUN-EXC-3"
  ],
  "provenance": {
    "type": "spec",
    "note": "The two exports permit only the value redistributable. The reading rd has no statement, so its bytes are withheld (BUN-RED-4), and the device store keeps rd without bytes. The new excerpt ex has a statement with the value redistributable, so the delta bundle has its bytes. The reading rd is in the base closure and is the parent of ex. Rule 3 of BUN-DLT-2 lists the withheld digest of rd in the bundle, because the check of BUN-EXC-3 reads the bytes of the parent. BUN-IMP-9 defers that check, so the import is ok, as for the bundle of the same request with no base context (BUN-DLT-5). A device context has the full closure of s2."
  },
